-- title:
--   Product joint law of the current Lévy reserve and the entire continuous-time future increment path
-- statement:
--   Under the original spectrally negative Lévy process model with full filtration F, fix a time s. Suppose that for every finite set I of future nonnegative times, the sigma algebra jointly generated by the shifted future increments X_(s+t)−X_s for t∈I is independent of F_s. Then the JOINT DISTRIBUTION of the current real state X_s and the ENTIRE future shifted increment process (t≥0)↦X_(s+t)−X_s is EXACTLY the product measure of their two marginal laws. This is a full uncountable-time path-space product law, not just a two-time or grid formula. The proof uses accepted chat04_whole_future_process_indep_past_of_finite_cylinders UUID e87d68dd-58e9-4570-8c43-ece958416b16, adaptedness to make X_s F_s-measurable, sigma-algebra monotonicity to transfer independence from F_s to X_s, and pinned Mathlib IndepFun.map_prod_eq_prod_map_map. It provides the Markov state/future-path distribution factorisation required for killed barrier payoff integrals. The finite-cylinder premise remains a separate nontrivial obligation and killed q-scale harmonicity is not implied.
-- source:
--   ACCEPTED full process independence from F_s UUID e87d68dd-58e9-4570-8c43-ece958416b16; pinned ProbabilityTheory.IndepFun_iff_Indep and IndepFun.map_prod_eq_prod_map_map, original Levy adaptedness.

import Mathlib.Probability.Independence.Basic
import Mathlib.Probability.Independence.Process.Basic
import Definitions.Def_AvramDividend_Classical_SpectrallyNegativeLevy
import Theorems.Thm_AvramDividend_Classical_chat04_whole_future_process_indep_past_of_finite_cylinders

open MeasureTheory ProbabilityTheory
open scoped NNReal ENNReal
open AvramDividend.Classical

theorem AvramDividend.Classical.chat04_full_future_path_reserve_product_law
    {Ω : Type*} [mΩ : MeasurableSpace Ω] {P : Measure Ω}
    {𝓕 : Filtration ℝ≥0 mΩ}
    (X : SpectrallyNegativeLevy P 𝓕)
    (s : ℝ≥0)
    (hFinite : ∀ I : Finset ℝ≥0,
      Indep (⨆ t ∈ I, MeasurableSpace.comap
        (fun ω => X.X (s + t) ω - X.X s ω) inferInstance)
        (𝓕 s) P) :
    Measure.map
      (fun ω => (X.X s ω,
        fun t : ℝ≥0 => X.X (s + t) ω - X.X s ω)) P =
      (Measure.map (X.X s) P).prod
        (Measure.map (fun ω => fun t : ℝ≥0 =>
          X.X (s + t) ω - X.X s ω) P) := by sorry
